(3771063, 526685, 67841, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by shamer:</b></div><hr/><i> awesome find (or idea?) but horrible bokeh!   The far back has great color, but the near background is unpleasing... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Boy, I sorta sound like a jerk there - ha ha!  I really dug those background colors &amp; the shadow, but for whatever reason, my eye was fixated on those red highlights &amp; box-blur nature of the bokeh here.  Hey, I still voted a 5 on it (better than a lot in this challenge - let''s just say I generously used both ends of the voting spectrum...).  I think all those little bits made the image a little too busy for me - this would be an excellent candidate for selectively softening while adding heavy doses of dodging/burning to get the composition down to it''s core imagery.</td>', 'Originally posted by shamer: awesome find (or idea?) but horrible bokeh!   The far back has great color, but the near background is unpleasing...   Boy, I sorta sound like a jerk there - ha ha!  I really dug those background colors & the shadow, but for whatever reason, my eye was fixated on those red highlights & box-blur nature of the bokeh here.  Hey, I still voted a 5 on it (better than a lot in this challenge - let''s just say I generously used both ends of the voting spectrum...).  I think all those little bits made the image a little too busy for me - this would be an excellent candidate for selectively softening while adding heavy doses of dodging/burning to get the composition down to it''s core imagery.', '2007-06-12 00:14:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(3771133, 527597, 60862, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the high score and placement, Neil!</td>', 'Congrats on the high score and placement, Neil!', '2007-06-12 00:25:19.000000', NULL, 0),
